    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But that's the thing, it doesn't feel like a \"fresh perspective.\" It feels like the end of the book. When a piece of music reaches its final cadence, you don't just keep playing random notes to keep the sound going—that would ruin the work. It's beautiful because it ends. I look in the mirror and I don't see a \"creative endeavor\" anymore, I just see someone waiting for the inevitable decay. I don't want to be the person watching the music fade into static.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
